Licensing scope — AI Character Assets

This is a private, noncommercial archive of unofficial fan-character artwork.
There is no blanket MIT grant over this repository's illustrations, character
designs, embedded/transformed image copies, or third-party brand marks.

DeepSeek whale-girl adaptations: retain credit to 上善无形 / 上善 (initial
character design) and ZipZipPipe (DeepSeek maid redesign). Insofar as the
maintainer holds licensable rights in these adaptations, those contributions
follow Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International.
See LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt and NOTICE.md. No additional restriction is
placed on rights that recipients already have under that license.

Claude and GPT original character references: ZipZipPipe's AI娘化 collection
requires attribution and noncommercial use. The original statement's specific
CC BY-NC-SA clause concerns DeepSeek; this archive does not purport to grant
a CC license over Claude/GPT references on the original author's behalf.
Those materials and their adaptations retain the applicable upstream rights.

Logos, product names and other trademarks remain with their respective owners.
Artwork licenses do not grant trademark rights or imply endorsement.

Mixed previews, layered images and archives retain the applicable rights of
their constituent material. Inclusion in a PNG, ZIP, script or data structure
does not relicense underlying artwork. No commercial permission is granted.

Any grant is limited to rights the granting party actually holds. The private
repository setting is an access choice and does not remove existing Creative
Commons rights of authorized recipients. Public redistribution or commercial
use requires a separate review of the applicable original terms and rights.

Scripts and documentation are retained for archival/reproducibility purposes;
this archive does not announce a new public software license for them.
